In a long PDF document this method may take a little while to return data, which could possibly result in an "impatient" user pressing the copy-shortcut multiple times.

That would result in bad performance, hence I'd suggest that we make sure that this method can't be called until a previous invocation has returned its data. The easiest solution is probably to make use of a flag (which we obviously also reset at the end of the method):
```suggestion
  async getAllText() {
    if (this.#getAllTextInProgress) {
      throw new Error("getAllText already in progress.");
    }
    this.#getAllTextInProgress = true;
```
